  "question": {
    "text": "<p>A spool of mass <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>M</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>kg</mi></math> and radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>20</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> has an axle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>r</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi>cm</mi></math> around which a string is wrapped. The moment of inertia about an axis perpendicular to the plane of the spool and passing through the centre is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi>M</mi><msup><mi>R</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></mrow><mn>2</mn></mfrac></math>.&nbsp;If the coefficient of friction between the surface and the spool is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>0</mn><mo>.</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp;then the maximum tension which can be applied to the string for which the spool doesn't slip, is&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced close=\"]\" open=\"[\"><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn><mo>&nbsp;</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi><mo>&nbsp;</mo><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">s</mi><mrow><mo>-</mo><mn>2</mn></mrow></msup></mrow></mfenced></math></p>\r\r<p><img alt=\"\" src=\"assets\\qt0037_77d9f9e02062.jpg\" style=\"width: 180px; height: 147px;\" /></p>\r"
  },
